==Strategy==
Stalling is the name of the game for this Otherworld Colosseum; the hyperbuffed Cat Cannon deals 910,000 damage per cast, effectively clearing out the entire field every time it's used. Naturally, you'll want to use it as much as possible to take full advantage of the buff. This means using Recharge Speed (M) [[Cat Combo]]s like [[Sweets (Combo)|Sweets]] to cut it down to ''35 seconds''. Don't bother overdosing on Recharge Speed Combos since there's a hardcap minimum at 31.67 seconds, so keep it to one Medium or Large Combo.

You're easily able to stall out the opening wave of peons and clear them out with your Cat Cannon to buy yourself as much time as you want before triggering the boss wave. Your Cat Cannon deals almost enough damage to instantly kill R.Ost and Commander Ostromeda on {{1c}}, so wait until both are on screen to use it. Stall them out with [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] as well as other small meatshields while chipping them with [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cats]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]. The General GreGories have a Barrier that prevents your Cat Cannon from killing them instantly, so bring [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] to stop them right in their tracks until your Cat Cannon recharges. You win once you kill the second Commander Ostromeda.

